# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.backup.py
venv/
.venv/
env/
*.egg-info/

# --- Secrets & keys: NEVER commit these ---
# If any of these are already tracked in git history, deleting them here is
# NOT enough - they must be purged from history and the credentials rotated,
# since anything ever pushed to GitHub must be treated as compromised even
# after removal.
.env
.env.*
api_key.txt
*_key
*_key.*
*.pem
*.ppk
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*.key
!requirements.txt

# --- Caches / local DBs (regenerated at runtime) ---
*.db
soccerbase_cache*.db
results_cache.db

# --- Logs & debug output ---
*.log
debug.log
_diag_out.txt

# --- Ad-hoc / dated output files (predictions, reports, telegram previews) ---
# These are pipeline OUTPUT, not source. If you want prediction history
# tracked in git, keep prediction_history.json (already handled explicitly
# by the GitHub Actions workflow) rather than dozens of per-day snapshots.
predictions_soccerbase_*.json
predictions_*.json
home_win_predictions_*.json
*_report_*.json
*_report_*.txt
*_vip_report_*.txt
*_telegram*.txt
*_body.txt
*_output*.txt
*_errors.txt
*_today*.txt
selected_results_report.txt
combined_free.txt
combined_vip.txt
telegram_daily.txt

# --- OS / editor cruft ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Local run output (NOT committed) ---
# run_local.bat redirects each predictor's stdout to these files; the actual
# per-market Telegram section files are *_telegram.txt which are also ephemeral
# but are consumed by build_telegram_daily.py. The data files below are
# machine-specific and must not be pushed.
ou.txt
hw.txt
btts.txt
telegram.txt
*_telegram.txt
_diag_out.txt
_diag_err.txt
soccerbase_cache*.zip

# --- GitHub Actions self-hosted runner ---
# NEVER commit a runner folder to git. It contains:
#   - The .runner file with your repository URL + the runner registration token
#     (expires after 1 hour but should still not be exposed)
#   - .credentials and .credentials_rsaparams which hold the runner's
#     long-lived OAuth access token for this repository
#   - The run listener binaries and ~300MB of externals (Node runtime etc.)
#
# Best practice: keep the runner OUTSIDE your project entirely, e.g.
#   Good: C:\Inno Project\actions-runner\   (sibling of over-under)
#   Avoid: C:\Inno Project\over-under\actions-runner\  (inside repo)
#
# If you must keep it inside the repo for convenience, the lines below
# will at least prevent git from ever staging it.
actions-runner/
actions-runner-local/
_runner*/
.runner
.credentials
.credentials_rsaparams
*.service
.diag/
_work/

